Make dumbpipe use the OS trust store, and any proxy the environment names.

iroh defaults to a compiled-in copy of Mozilla's roots
(`CaTlsConfig::EmbeddedWebPki`). Behind a TLS-intercepting egress proxy the
relay presents the proxy's certificate, which chains to a CA only the system
knows about -- so a stock build reaches NO relay ("Failed to connect to the
home relay") on a host where curl and git work perfectly. `CaTlsConfig::system()`
is iroh's own answer; dumbpipe simply never calls it.

This changes the RELAY HOP ONLY. Payloads stay end-to-end encrypted between
endpoint keys: the relay could not read them before and cannot now.

`iroh-relay` becomes a direct dependency because `iroh` re-exports RelayConfig
and RelayMap but not CaTlsConfig. Both it and rustls-platform-verifier are
already in Cargo.lock as transitive entries, so no new crate is vendored.

